users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#pullrequestreview-5530982817","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#pullrequestreview-5530982817"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663"}},"submitted_at":"2026-10-15T09:32:03Z","commit_id":"64c9ffb2f2fecdccdc72fb811f827c2baa5b581f"},{"id":5531371495,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSbIH5w","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?u=2b8b17ce969861380874563b333a546e0bbaab56&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We discussed this in core meeting.\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce did mention that we should consider waiting until we have evidence users were making this mistake.\r\n\r\nHe also suggested this could also use a generalised allocation warning system (perhaps in `ObjectDB`) but that would be easy to change at a later date, and we usually prefer localized solutions prior to generalizing.\r\n\r\nWe have to also be aware that users might not be as versed in the downsides of allocations than c++ contributors, so any help they can get in this area is useful.\r\n\r\nProviding hints in the script editor would be in many ways even better, but that only seems possible in the near term for GDScript, whereas this problem is likely to be worse case in C# with garbage collection.\r\n\r\nApproval on technical principle here, leave it for others to decide on wording, and leave up to production whether they prefer to wait until 4.9 / get more info from the new availability of the non-allocating physics functions.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#pullrequestreview-5531371495","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#pullrequestreview-5531371495"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663"}},"submitted_at":"2026-10-15T10:00:44Z","commit_id":"64c9ffb2f2fecdccdc72fb811f827c2baa5b581f"}]